.SH NAME
amslogprt \- UNIX utility program for printing AMS log messages from amslog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBamslogprt\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBamslogprt\fR simply reads AMS activity log messages from standard input
(nominally written by \fBamslog\fR and prints them.  When the content of a
logged message is judged not to be an ASCII text string, the content is
printed in hexadecimal.
.PP
\&\fBamslogprt\fR terminates at the end of input.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBamslogprt\fR terminated normally.
